      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does `CachingAuthTokenAccessor`, which should be a wrapper around the `DirectAuthTokentAccessor`, inherit any logic from the `AbstractAuthTokenAccessor`.\nWhat if this class simply delegates all calls to the wrapped instance of the `DirectAuthTokentAccessor` and in addition takes care to always read via the cache and to evict from the cache whenever something is modified. Wouldn\u0027t that work?",
      "revId": "9684c6f8c386a7e85c82b5d1ffc87719d2980367",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8af4ddfb_d6ecaabb",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/CachingAuthTokenAccessor.java",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
