      "writtenOn": "2025-04-16T13:26:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`commit()` is a private method only being used by the `DirectAuthTokenAccessor`. The only way Icould imagine this to work, is to reimplement all public methods of the diretc accessor in the cached accessor, in which I call the wrapped direct accessor and then do the eviction. But IMO that is also quite ugly.",
      "parentUuid": "9d44ea66_8eebc726",
      "revId": "9684c6f8c386a7e85c82b5d1ffc87719d2980367",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fee0f9a8_8ba02727",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/CachingAuthTokenAccessor.java",
