      "writtenOn": "2025-04-17T10:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The only way Icould imagine this to work, is to reimplement all public methods of the diretc accessor in the cached accessor, in which I call the wrapped direct accessor ...\n\nThis is exactly how delegation pattern works. Java doesn\u0027t have language level support for delegation so we have to code it.\nHowever, IMO with this approach we gain clarity in design as we use composition (instead of inheritance) to build (caching accessor) from more basic parts: direct accessor and the cache.",
      "parentUuid": "2f03a1ff_2a7db998",
      "revId": "9684c6f8c386a7e85c82b5d1ffc87719d2980367",
